(Section 2: Corporate Travel and Expense Reimbursements) '
(Domestic travel meal per diem: $75 per day flat per diem for approved domestic travel requiring overnight lodging.) '
(International maritime travel meal per diem: $110 per day flat per diem for international port assignments.) '
(Hotel lodging expense limit: Maximum $200 per night for standard tier cities and $280 per night for designated coastal port cities.) '
(Personal vehicle mileage allowance: $0.67 per mile for pre-authorized business travel.) '
(Travel expense reporting deadline: Complete expense reports and itemized receipts must be submitted within 14 calendar days of travel.) '
(Emergency travel evacuation coverage: Company provides up to $100,000 emergency medical evacuation coverage during international business travel.) '
ET
endstream
